      ":question/id": "eed86cf8-361a-5183-810e-cdf192a18282",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/99/99572547820ce2939515e8e93bd4b7b08800f3c94cb8663aa4689b23241a4def.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, ending at $A$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &=1\\,(2, 0)=(2, 0). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{AC} &=(0, 4).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/97/97968f79bede28e482151e2bdff3ca5b7d77f445d81cd867c5cfdac573cba435.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(0, 2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{4}{2}=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{AC}=2\\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AC} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=2$."
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186735413,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "19d54211-ff5f-5051-905e-9afef9a388d8",
              ":answer/type": {
                ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
              },
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{3}{4}",
