      ":question/difficulty": {
        ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/hard"
      },
      ":question/id": "0686d6db-4b3e-5c05-9b47-6ef494a7f1e2",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/10/10bc9ef3424bcffdb9fc3958f3885062d2a026d1199477cb2ac3621933560ead.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(3, -2)=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -1\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(3, -3).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/94/941dc7de7d4ec7ba07c82bf076a4835dfb79683a5eda4525c20ef5b88e65331c.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(4, -4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{3}{4} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-3}{-4}=\\frac{3}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\frac{3}{4}\\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{4}\\mathbf{b} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{4}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{3}{4}$."
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186735416,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
