      ":question/id": "31fe6aa1-ed1c-5040-a39d-dbc385628868",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/e6/e639cf6dcd4133ab8c3f858621c4c02c4018a56ec8430efcbd592b10d6b20eac.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, ending at $A$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &=1\\,(2, 0)=(2, 0). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{AC} &=(0, -2).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/c6/c63704ec4b7fbd93dc0d104d08bf906cb9d278e66afb0fc3568932b11cd0aaee.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(0, -4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-2}{-4}=\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{AC}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AC} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{1}{2}$."
    },
