      ":question/id": "d5700f14-a6e6-5fb8-9246-58b54d4f05ea",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/07/07544617f045a6221325a956583b5c3f8821ddf7ef1ca08f2c9fb4e9cf209a16.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, ending at $B$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &=1\\,(0, -5)=(0, -5). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{BC} &=(8, 0).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/c8/c839ff25040105b01838169fd12e0508ba4c6c07d314616ba96d98fe185b7581.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(4, 0)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{8}{4}=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{BC}=2\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OB}+\\overrightarrow{BC} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{b}+2\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=2$."
    },
