      ":question/id": "07c2b492-d44f-5131-9a7b-db9206a3e7e1",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/87/870ab808de9f829e5967f4792119b4b596ad9de28ff714e1ce5c3b2b686338fb.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{4}{3}\\,(3, 0)=(4, 0). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(4, -8).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/80/808f2835fcaf678e3cbde7898ac8af3893e9dc71ed879cff900aefc430393c74.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(2, -4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{4}{2}=2 \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-8}{-4}=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=2\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}+2\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=2$."
    },
