      ":question/id": "0b0bfae0-92ed-5b58-bac6-9ee6206c2d11",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/5f/5f32d62f2c3f23418be558580cc601f78c8a14154a77f805d58da57fcf0e49e7.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, ending at $B$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &=1\\,(0, -3)=(0, -3). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{BC} &=(5, -10).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/5e/5e02968249ec36c4a1f3135bbffd984f2822275c0f2fb51b477a3ac4412b43e3.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(2, -4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-10}{-4}=\\frac{5}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{BC}=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OB}+\\overrightarrow{BC} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{b}+\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{5}{2}$."
    },
