      ":question/id": "5b880935-6ff4-54af-834b-282c8fffc65e",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/5e/5e81fc8d41121ddfde878e3ba0aec7531eb29901282786e1915a408ae5e6af01.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $3\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=3\\,(2, -2)=(6, -6). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(-4, 0).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/f5/f571ab2db29957aa8533bfb6fb602fb5c061fffb2d996ee60d6f8279e2fb19d9.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(-2, 0)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{-4}{-2}=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=2\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{b}+2\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=2$."
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186761427,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/choices": [
