      ":question/id": "a27601af-a5b2-5b2c-bf35-e7d92d0686b2",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/c1/c17a5d06bf0ff0b67565880092c6dbdcd085d1460b610f35634f649c88b77998.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{4}{3}\\,(3, 0)=(4, 0). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(4, -4).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/e6/e6f785f03744709ff1340cc3f6fdad62001df775a1f2972fbd6796844c358875.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(4, -4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{4}{4}=1 \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-4}{-4}=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}+\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=1$."
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186761436,
