      ":question/id": "c5f7f6d8-ab59-58b4-be81-e566ab6dfb18",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/62/62f920be0ea00c893a287d49095f3951c338d308a339fd65c4b5c739faf8d331.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{4}{3}\\,(3, 0)=(4, 0). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(6, 6).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/c8/c8f9055a336a6751224473a371de86577ae3b6c63bed897612b487dd64a7c905.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(2, 2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{6}{2}=3 \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{6}{2}=3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=3\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}+3\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=3$."
    },
