      ":question/id": "0b52761a-f97c-5a5e-9091-24a269d3503d",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/9b/9ba36afbf950658168bc518a816644c166d5ff5ab0a94211801e5671d31f3c11.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{3}{2}\\,(-2, -3)=\\left(-3, -\\frac{9}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(-4, -2).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/c6/c6b86b252674f7d90646938ae31c3a0da85d333d3bc85d39158b2797289748f8.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(-4, -2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{-4}{-4}=1 \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-2}{-2}=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}+\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=1$."
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186761459,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
