      ":question/id": "50582b9b-ef2c-561c-87b1-56056b9736e4",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/a5/a5ed245562242fd0250788abba50ad1590d135c370df6ca859f4c685de025969.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(-3, -1)=\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}, -\\frac{1}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=\\left(-\\frac{7}{2}, -\\frac{7}{2}\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/f3/f34061f5ffb1c2aaab8728cb51f3dc88df57e1c483e2fae478eb659c220284d2.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(-2, -2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{-\\frac{7}{2}}{-2}=\\frac{7}{4} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-\\frac{7}{2}}{-2}=\\frac{7}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}+\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\frac{7}{4}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{7}{4}$."
    },
