      ":question/id": "73ab5e8d-2110-5e36-a0eb-6978303037b8",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/ba/baa813bfb835f8d56faf0fbbf33de2710d6aa4d2f08e1c8c0038bb3124c34cf3.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(3, 1)=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=\\left(\\frac{5}{2}, \\frac{5}{2}\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/9d/9de04a873bbf94f85e2d53a0afec52a1c9c78ee6f4f8f748f2402f35bd0dad4c.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(2, 2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{\\frac{5}{2}}{2}=\\frac{5}{4} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{\\frac{5}{2}}{2}=\\frac{5}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\frac{5}{4}\\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{4}\\mathbf{b} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{4}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{5}{4}$."
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186761463,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
