      ":question/id": "8b1cfdff-acd8-5881-b037-06fb5dc8fe29",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/6b/6b053cd19e77620430bfbeb259117c965ce2420455de9363db687f02f6f142d4.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{5}{2}\\,(2, -3)=\\left(5, -\\frac{15}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(4, -8).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/13/13b64631f34fdd5cc14f6c14e02de127f40bcea8232f1e3ef191fe07a77403e8.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(2, -4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{4}{2}=2 \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-8}{-4}=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=2\\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b} \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=2$."
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186761464,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
