      ":question/id": "9bbf6a60-e451-5c35-959a-002bf889e0d2",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/65/65f1cf69502cf5650f9bface4f5bddd453b2abac588cba228aadb66806f27397.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{1}{2}\\,(-1, 3)=\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{3}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(-1, 1).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/31/31a3b382de27d55a5ececfc928c4a57c3772af8031da56565f31c2d840a2943b.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(-4, 4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{-1}{-4}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{b} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{1}{4}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{1}{4}$."
    },
