      ":question/difficulty": {
        ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/hard"
      },
      ":question/id": "e17bae6c-eab8-59aa-b469-d0c593dcc8be",
      ":question/problem": "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\n![](images/dd/dd759f3e9127fccdf2f2ec70f72574888319844368ae1d7ad9e2088948092b2a.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Construct the known component $\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{5}{2}\\,(1, 1)=\\left(\\frac{5}{2}, \\frac{5}{2}\\right). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(1, 2).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/13/133edd8147d930d3ad98473e06db0121fe43ca2ea91870a4ff91470db3dafcbf.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(2, 4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{2}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{1}{2}$."
    },
    {
